{
  "id": "b1-u02-grammar",
  "unit": "b1-u02",
  "title": "Used to, was going to, should have",
  "seoTitle": "Used to, was going to, should have in Turkish",
  "intro": "This unit adds four more members to the family of [B1 unit 1](gp-di-compounds), all built the same way: a tense, the past `-DI`, a type II ending. The past aorist `-(I)rdI` tells old habits, *Eskiden burada otururduk* (We used to live here); `-(y)AcAktI` tells plans that fell through, *Seni arayacaktım* (I was going to call you); `-mAlIydI` and `-(y)AbilIrdI` look back at what should or could have happened. Last, *-mAk üzere* says that something is about to happen.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "point": "gp-used-to",
      "title": "Otururduk: used to",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Put the [aorist](gp-aorist-forms) in the past and you get **used to**: *otururuz* (we live) → *otururduk* (we used to live). The aorist keeps all its forms, `-r`, `-Ar` or `-Ir`, including the thirteen verbs in `-Ir` (*gelirdim, alırdım, bilirdim*). After r the D is d. Turkish grammars call it *geniş zamanın hikâyesi*."
        },
        {
          "type": "rule",
          "label": "Past aorist",
          "lines": [
            "stem + aorist -r / -Ar / -Ir + -dI + -m / -n / -∅ / -k / -nIz / -lAr",
            "oku- → okurdum       yap- → yapardım",
            "gel- → gelirdim      çalış- → çalışırdım",
            "negative: stem + -mAz + -dI → gelmezdim"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paradigm",
          "title": "*gelmek* (to come)",
          "rows": [
            {
              "p": "ben",
              "tr": "gel|ir|di|m",
              "en": "I used to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "sen",
              "tr": "gel|ir|di|n",
              "en": "you used to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "o",
              "tr": "gel|ir|di",
              "en": "he or she used to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "biz",
              "tr": "gel|ir|di|k",
              "en": "we used to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "siz",
              "tr": "gel|ir|di|niz",
              "en": "you used to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "onlar",
              "tr": "gel|ir|ler|di",
              "en": "they used to come"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "**Negative.** The present aorist has *gelmem* and *gelmeyiz* for **I** and **we**. The past keeps *-mAz* in every person: *gelmezdim*, *gelmezdik*."
        },
        {
          "type": "paradigm",
          "title": "*gelmek*, negative",
          "rows": [
            {
              "p": "ben",
              "tr": "gel|mez|di|m",
              "en": "I didn't use to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "sen",
              "tr": "gel|mez|di|n",
              "en": "you didn't use to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "o",
              "tr": "gel|mez|di",
              "en": "he or she didn't use to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "biz",
              "tr": "gel|mez|di|k",
              "en": "we didn't use to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "siz",
              "tr": "gel|mez|di|niz",
              "en": "you didn't use to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "onlar",
              "tr": "gel|mez|ler|di",
              "en": "they didn't use to come"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paradigm",
          "title": "*gelmek*, question",
          "rows": [
            {
              "p": "ben",
              "tr": "gel|ir mi|y|di|m",
              "en": "did I use to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "sen",
              "tr": "gel|ir mi|y|di|n",
              "en": "did you use to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "o",
              "tr": "gel|ir mi|y|di",
              "en": "did he or she use to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "biz",
              "tr": "gel|ir mi|y|di|k",
              "en": "did we use to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "siz",
              "tr": "gel|ir mi|y|di|niz",
              "en": "did you use to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "onlar",
              "tr": "gel|ir|ler mi|y|di",
              "en": "did they use to come"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "It tells what happened regularly in the past, often with *eskiden* (formerly), *o zamanlar* (back then), *çocukken* (as a child) or *her yaz* (every summer). Like English **would**, it can carry a whole memory: *Pazarları anneanneme giderdik. Anneannem börek yapardı, biz bahçede oynardık.* (On Sundays we would go to my grandmother's. She would make börek, and we would play in the garden.)"
        },
        {
          "type": "examples",
          "items": [
            {
              "tr": "Eskiden burada otururduk.",
              "seg": "Eskiden burada otur|ur|du|k.",
              "en": "We used to live here."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Çocukken her yaz köye giderdik.",
              "seg": "Çocukken her yaz köye gid|er|di|k.",
              "en": "As children we used to go to the village every summer."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Babam her sabah gazete okurdu.",
              "seg": "Babam her sabah gazete oku|r|du.",
              "en": "My father used to read the paper every morning."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Eskiden kahve içmezdim, şimdi her gün içiyorum.",
              "seg": "Eskiden kahve iç|mez|di|m, şimdi her gün içiyorum.",
              "en": "I didn't use to drink coffee; now I drink it every day."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Annen sana masal anlatır mıydı?",
              "seg": "Annen sana masal anlat|ır mı|y|dı?",
              "en": "Did your mother use to tell you stories?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "tip",
          "title": "Three pasts",
          "text": "*Her yaz köye giderdik*: a habit, **we used to go**. *O yaz köyde kalıyorduk*: the scene, **we were staying**. *O yaz köye gittik*: one event, **we went**. States need no special form: *Eskiden burada bir fırın vardı* (There used to be a bakery here)."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "compare",
          "text": "English **used to** and **would** both map to `-(I)rdI`. The past continuous `-(I)yordu` is also heard for habits (*Her yaz köye gidiyorduk*), as the French imparfait is, but `-(I)rdI` is the usual choice when you look back on a habit."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "tip",
          "title": "Would",
          "text": "`-(I)rdI` is also the **would** of polite wishes and of unreal conditions, which [B2 unit 1](gp-unreal-present) explains: *Çok isterdim* (I'd love to, or I'd have loved to)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "point": "gp-future-in-past",
      "title": "Arayacaktım: was going to",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "The [future](gp-future) `-(y)AcAk` + `-DI` gives **was going to**: *arayacaktım* (I was going to call). After k the D is t, and the k doesn't soften, because a consonant follows it. Turkish grammars call it *gelecek zamanın hikâyesi*."
        },
        {
          "type": "rule",
          "label": "Future in the past",
          "lines": ["stem + -(y)AcAk + -tI + -m / -n / -∅ / -k / -nIz / -lAr", "gel- → gelecektim     ara- → arayacaktım", "git- → gidecektim     ye-  → yiyecektim"]
        },
        {
          "type": "paradigm",
          "title": "*gelmek* (to come)",
          "rows": [
            {
              "p": "ben",
              "tr": "gel|ecek|ti|m",
              "en": "I was going to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "sen",
              "tr": "gel|ecek|ti|n",
              "en": "you were going to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "o",
              "tr": "gel|ecek|ti",
              "en": "he or she was going to come"
            },
            {
              "p": "biz",
