        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "pitfall",
          "title": "Should have, must have",
          "text": "*Gelmeliydi* is **he should have come**, and suggests he didn't. A confident guess about the past, **he must have come**, is a different form, *gelmiş olmalı*, in [C1 unit 1](gp-mis-olmali)."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "tip",
          "text": "For a past obligation that was simply met, use *zorundaydım* or *zorunda kaldım* from [A2 unit 6](gp-zorunda): *Erken kalkmak zorunda kaldım* (I had to get up early)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "point": "gp-could-have",
      "title": "Gelebilirdin, gelemezdim: could have, couldn't have",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Ability has two pasts of this kind. `-(y)Abil` + the aorist *-ir* + `-DI` gives *gelebilirdim*: **I could have come**, or **I was able to come** in general. Inability `-(y)AmA` + *-z* + `-DI` gives *gelemezdim*: **I couldn't have come**, or **I never could come**. Both follow [A2 unit 5](gp-abil): *bil* never changes, and the inability form has no *bil* at all."
        },
        {
          "type": "rule",
          "label": "Could have, couldn't have",
          "lines": ["stem + -(y)Abil + -ir + -di + ending → gelebilirdim", "stem + -(y)A + -mAz + -dI + ending   → gelemezdim", "yap- → yapabilirdim / yapamazdım"]
        },
        {
          "type": "paradigm",
          "title": "*gelmek*: could have",
          "rows": [
